WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.040
2024

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:07.360
As old conflicts rumble on, and new threats emerge,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.480
one image, more than any other will be replicated around the globe

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.760
In a year that will see the biggest display of democracy in history

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.800
what else will the next 12 months bring?

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.880
Here are some of the stories set to shape the world ahead

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.400
2024 will be the biggest election year in history

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.800
More than half of the world’s population live in countries

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.320
holding national elections

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.640
But there are two elections in particular that could have

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.920
huge repercussions worldwide

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.120
One is the most powerful democracy in the world

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.960
The other is a small, self-governing island

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.080
less than 200km off the coast of China

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.800
The election in Taiwan in January matters

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.680
because the island’s future is so uncertain

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.720
According to US intelligence, President Xi Jinping wants his 

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.640
armed forces to be ready for an invasion by 2027

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.680
Taiwan is a geopolitical flashpoint

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.080
An invasion by China could lead to war with America

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.240
So the stakes are high for whoever wins power

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.320
in both Taiwan and America

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.240
The strategy they pursue could deter a Chinese invasion—

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.320
or hasten it

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:38.080
On the island itself the threat—for some—is already tangible

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.400
More than half of Taiwanese citizens do not have confidence

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.640
in their government’s ability to defend against an invasion from China

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.160
Well of course you have to know

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.800
what the wound is to treat it

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:55.760
Some citizens are even taking civil-defence workshops,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.840
including 22-year-old Chen Buo Yen

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.680
With regard to the possibility of war,

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.680
it’s best to be as prepared as you can be

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.920
It would be a lie to say that I am not afraid

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.800
but I am prepared

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.160
And those concerns will be at the forefront of Taiwanese

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.720
voters’ minds when they head to the polls in January

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.800
Voters will be faced with a choice between the current ruling party

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.920
which emphasises Taiwanese self-rule 

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.040
and the need to resist Chinese bullying

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:36.160
And two opposition parties, keen to pursue warmer relations

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.560
Supporters of the current government claim the opposition

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.160
would make it easier for China to ultimately take over Taiwan

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.640
And on the other hand,

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.600
the opposition camp thinks that

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.040
the DPP government is going

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.960
to take Taiwan towards a path of

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.600
legal independence

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.560
And that will be a path to

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.640
eventual war with China

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.040
The likelihood of war won’t just depend on

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:05.880
what happens in Taiwan’s election, but in America’s too

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.160
Would you send the US military into Taiwan

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.320
if President Xi were to invade? President Biden says he would

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:13.960
I won’t say, I won’t say

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:19.200
A second Trump presidency would spell unpredictability

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.000
and mounting levels of risk

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.920
And not just for Taiwan, but for America and the rest of the world

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:41.920
In July, all eyes will be on Paris for the 2024 Olympic games

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.800
But while athletes battle it out on the ground,

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.960
spectators’ eyes might be drawn to the skies above

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.320
At first glance, it might be mistaken for a helicopter

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.640
But this is a supersized drone

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:59.000
And it could be the future of public transport

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.120
Known as eVTOLs

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.040
electric vertical, take-off and landing

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.080
They run entirely on batteries

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.840
making them a sustainable way to fly

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.400
Five years ago eVTOLs were only known to a very small group of people

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:17.200
that were really aviation geeks tinkering on new technologies

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.480
Over the last year or so, we’ve seen a lot of public test flights

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.400
and next year commercial service is the milestone

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.640
If all goes to plan, the Paris Olympics

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:28.680
will mark the start of commercial eVTOL flights

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.360
Volocopter, the company running the flights,

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.680
is hoping to transport tourists along five different routes

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:38.440
at speeds of up to 110kph

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.960
We believe if we can fly in Paris, we can fly anywhere

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.640
This is also a start into a new area of mobility

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:49.520
Allowing quiet, safe and sustainable vehicles 

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:52.760
to enter the city centres, which other vehicles can’t

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:55.200
The technology is evolving so rapidly

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:00.200
that aviation regulators are struggling to work out how to certify flights

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.720
Volocopter has had to roll back on its original plan

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.280
of pilotless, self-flying eVTOLs to try to appease the authorities

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.360
I think the only way to get certified right now and for the years to come  

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.200
is by offering a piloted version

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:20.360
It’s not technology that hinders us to go towards autonomy

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.840
It is certification and public acceptance

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:29.360
Volocopter is not the only company hoping to take off in 2024

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.160
Across the world, other companies are racing to the skies

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:38.280
in a market that could be worth $1trn by 2040

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.200
But while much of the industry will be commercial, 

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.240
some companies will be catering for those who prefer to go private

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.520
We’ve got two large wings

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.960
you’re getting all your lift from 

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:54.040
In 2024, Palo Alto startup Pivotal will be launching an eVTOL

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:57.800
anyone with deep enough pockets, can purchase and pilot themselves

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:01.120
With just one seat, it’s more of a flying motorbike

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.640
than a flying taxi

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.520
The feeling is pretty hard to describe

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.800
to see the world from up there

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.400
The company provides a few weeks of training

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.520
but you don’t need a pilot’s licence

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.800
As long as it’s only flown over rural land and during daylight

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.640
The Helix will be one of the most 

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:20.960
easy-to-learn-to-fly vehicles ever made

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.640
You need to use a single joystick to do

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.480
everything the aircraft can do

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.800
from takeoff to landing, 

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.640
to hover, to forward flight

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:35.800
Although, with a price-tag of $190,000, they’re not cheap

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:37.520
There is no denying

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:38.600
that it’s going to be used

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.320
principally for recreation to start

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:42.800
but it will grow from there

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.320
and it will become a new form of transportation

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:46.800
that we take for granted someday

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.600
I’m Tom Standage, editor of&lt;i&gt; The World Ahead&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:55.040
To read about the prospects for the coming year,

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.920
and get a head start on more of the trends and themes to watch,

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:00.560
why not take out a subscription to&lt;i&gt; The Economist&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:04.240
which includes full access to &lt;i&gt;The World Ahead&lt;/i&gt; 2024?

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.960
To get the best offer, click on the link

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:18.400
In 2024 the focus on AI won’t just be on what it can do

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.040
but how humans might control it

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.440
Some people are worried that if you impose strict rules too early

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.840
you stifle the technology

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.040
and other people are worried that if you don't move now

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:30.200
then there could be dangerous consequences

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.800
So far, much of the discussion around regulation

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.960
has been on the most powerful AI,

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.560
known as frontier models,

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.000
and the risks they could pose to humanity

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.960
But there's a danger that decision-makers are looking the wrong way

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.640
We should be focusing on the real immediate potential

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:50.320
but also the real immediate risks of this technology

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.520
which aren’t about killer robots

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:53.600
they’re about things like bias and discrimination

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.840
Many governments are less than transparent about

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:59.320
how they deploy AI in decision-making

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.840
In London, the charity the Public Law Project has been trying

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:07.120
to uncover how the British government is using algorithms

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.280
So we can see 28 tools 

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.280
that are currently being used by the Home Office

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.360
One of their projects examines the British government’s use of

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:23.160
machine learning, a form of AI, in its investigation of welfare fraud

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:26.400
People who were applying for welfare support,

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.000
all of the same nationality background,

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.760
they were having their benefits suspended

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:34.280
for a really long period of time

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.240
We were really concerned that some of these systems

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:40.440
might be operating in a way that’s discriminatory

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.520
There is precedent for this

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:45.720
In 2021, an AI welfare scandal

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.480
brought down the Dutch government

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:49.760
The tax service here in the Netherlands

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.680
was wrongfully accusing tens of thousands of families

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.960
that they were frauding with child benefits

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:59.040
And Australia's “Robodebt” scandal 

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.760
led to at least two suicides

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.600
Driven to despair by a soulless, automated debt collector

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.280
and a government who called them welfare cheats

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.440
There has been some movement 

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:13.240
in an attempt to mitigate near-term risks

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:18.000
The EU is expected to bring in its AI Act in 2024

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.360
There will also be two AI safety summits

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.600
One in South Korea and one in Paris

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:28.120
But if they are anything like the first safety summit

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.360
at Bletchley Park in 2023

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:34.960
their focus will be mostly on frontier models and existential risk

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:39.720
I think talking up these existential, theoretical future risks

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:43.160
is really just a way of hyping the technology overall

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.400
Elon Musk would like to sell you a

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.760
self-driving car that uses AI to drive itself

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.600
but he also says that AI is really, really dangerous

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:52.920
If we are not careful with creating artificial general intelligence

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.440
we could have potentially a catastrophic outcome

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:58.280
Some people go as far as to say that

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.520
this is actually a deliberate sort of

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.160
decoy trying to distract attention from the

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.400
real existing harms of AI systems

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.480
And it’s also a way of drawing attention

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:07.600
for the people who work in the field

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:10.560
to just how powerful and wonderful they are

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:11.320
They’re really saying

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.240
“I made this thing that could destroy the world

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:14.280
Aren’t I clever?”

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.880
In 2024 one of the world’s

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.040
overlooked greenhouse-gas emitters

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:28.400
will finally be in the spotlight

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.360
Until now, governments’ focus

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.480
has been on cleaning up the most visible polluters

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.480
like energy and transport

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.880
But in the coming year, attention

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:40.560
will turn towards industry

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:44.880
and the production of materials central to modern everyday life

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.800
Industry is often out of sight

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:50.960
unlike the cars we drive or the electricity that powers our homes

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.080
But, in fact, almost everything

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:55.200
that we need in our lives is made by industry

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.640
Factories and other industrial facilities

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:02.560
belch out vast amounts of greenhouse gases

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:05.560
Nearly 29% of all emissions

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.600
That’s the same amount as electricity generation

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.720
and almost double transport

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.280
A big part of the problem

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.520
is that some industrial processes

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.000
need high temperatures,

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.800
which at the moment rely on fossil fuels,

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.720
like coal and natural gas

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.480
That's been a real challenge

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.480
But that’s also turning into a real opportunity

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:28.200
for some innovators

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.600
Coolbrook is a Finnish startup

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.800
developing technology it thinks can bring the world

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:36.200
one step closer to green industry

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:38.200
Their rotodynamic heater

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.120
generates high temperatures using electricity

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.080
&lt;i&gt;This really is the heart and soul of the installation&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:46.640
&lt;i&gt;The gas goes around the doughnut multiple times&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.800
&lt;i&gt;and then exits from the other side&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:52.080
Which means with the use of renewable electricity,

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.960
it can power industry with entirely sustainable energy

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.040
What we want to do

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.600
is that we replace majority of fossil fuels in the industry,

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:02.280
and that is very much doable

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.200
After decades of development,

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:10.400
2024 is the year this technology will start being shipped to factories

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:12.560
It’s absolutely exciting times

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.640
The last ten years have been already

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.560
the time of intensive development,

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:18.200
and last two to three years

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.720
have really been the game-changer for us

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.240
What we have now seen is that the heavy industry

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.600
is really starting to move

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.760
Industry might be more willing to decarbonise

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.920
because of incoming regulation

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.520
In 2023, the European Union

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:36.080
introduced a carbon tax on imports

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:40.000
We’ll see how it actually plays out in 2024

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:43.320
We’re likely to see other big economies

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.240
the United States, the UK and Australia

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.480
come up with their own versions of a carbon tax

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.000
And this kind of regulation has spurred

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.840
the creation of other decarbonising technologies

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:58.600
A few startups have come up with new ways

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.920
of containing renewable energy

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.800
in sometimes what are called “rocks in a box”,

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.160
sort of small packages

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.200
that get very hot, retain the heat

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:09.520
and can release it on demand when a factory needs it

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:12.560
But industry can sometimes drag its feet

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.440
and questions remain about whether it can change fast enough

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.840
One of the obstacles to decarbonising heavy industry

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.160
is that the processes are very complicated

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.200
It can be expensive and involve investment

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:26.360
in new capital equipment which industry does not want to do

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.760
Factory bosses don’t like to shut down their factories

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:31.000
and replace the kit that they use

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.840
because of the dreams of environmentalism

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.040
It’s a bit like changing the wheels on a bus

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.040
while the bus is moving at full speed,

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.640
but that’s kind of what we have to do

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:53.120
In 2024, the American-led

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.960
world order is going to be challenged again

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:59.080
as a bloc of non-Western nations gets bigger

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.320
The BRICS, made up of Brazil,

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.200
Russia,

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:02.960
India,

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:03.640
China

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:06.800
and South Africa will add five new members

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:09.680
Individually, the BRICS are some of the most exciting

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.480
and biggest economies on the planet

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.400
China is the world’s second-biggest economy

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.080
India is growing rapidly

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:19.920
In 2024, the club of five will be joined by Egypt,

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:24.480
Ethiopia, Iran, Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:27.160
Argentina was also slated to join,

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.840
but that now looks unlikely

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:31.200
under its new president, Javier Milei

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:35.240
On paper, BRICS+ seems a formidable outfit

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.040
Together, its members account for

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:39.320
nearly half of the world’s population

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:41.040
and their share of GDP

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:44.160
is around 20% more than the G7,

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:47.080
a group of rich democracies allied to America

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:49.280
But in reality,

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.440
their power will depend on how well they get on

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.880
They don’t seem to have that much in common

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.120
They are very, very different economies

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:00.480
India is on a huge kick about green minerals

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:03.680
China seems to be driving its economy towards consumption

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:04.800
rather than investment

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.080
What’s more,

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:07.720
there have been recent skirmishes

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.760
between China’s and India’s armies

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.520
across their shared border

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:12.800
There’s also a chance

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.200
that we’ll have found out that the BRICS mean

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.640
very little other than a club

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:16.960
for people to discuss things

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:19.760
But what’s really interesting about all these countries

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:21.440
that are joining next year

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.800
is that they’re the countries that have had

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.760
some of the most strained relations

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:27.320
with the West and its financial order

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:30.000
This global financial system was created

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.280
in the ashes of the second world war

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:35.160
At Bretton Woods, 44 nations

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.840
gathered to establish a new

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:39.280
international monetary and financial order

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:40.920
with America at the helm

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:44.160
What’s significant about the expansion of BRICS

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.560
is that it challenges this American-led world order

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.280
The most important thing about the BRICS

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.680
has always been that America isn’t invited

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:54.560
and there are ways in which the BRICS are using

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:57.240
that American-dominated financial system

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.200
and trying to twist it to their own advantage

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:02.160
The BRICS have created their own alternative

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.280
to the World Bank

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:05.240
and their own currency swap lines

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.400
in which countries agree

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.520
to swap different currencies,

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.680
countering the influence of the IMF

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.680
and its currency of choice,

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:13.560
the dollar

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.560
And it’s not just

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:17.920
America’s global economic influence

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.840
that is being challenged by the rise

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:21.080
of middle powers

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.680
The world is changing and America’s influence is declining

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:26.520
America is also a security power,

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.680
and its military is far superior

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.680
to any other countries in the world

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:33.320
But increasingly, there are several smaller,

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.480
rich countries that are playing the role

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:36.960
of the world’s negotiator

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.400
In the war in Ukraine, much of the

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:41.680
mediation has been done by Turkey

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.920
And in the war in Gaza,

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.080
by Qatar

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:49.000
America’s power is unlikely

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.200
to be eclipsed anytime soon

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:52.640
Its network of allies

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:54.760
is still much bigger than China’s

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.080
But in 2024,

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:00.280
expect the world to become more multipolar

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:03.000
as middle powers flex their muscles

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:05.920
Thanks for watching

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.960
To read more of our coverage of the coming year,

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:08.760
click the link

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:10.040
and don’t forget to subscribe

